# AICL Example: Industrial IoT
# Industrial IoT platform with SCADA integration, predictive maintenance, digital twin simulation,
# safety instrumented systems, and OPC-UA protocol support for smart manufacturing.

Goal: Build an industrial IoT platform that integrates with SCADA systems, provides predictive
    maintenance through ML models, maintains digital twins for simulation and optimization,
    enforces safety instrumented system protocols, and communicates via OPC-UA standards.

Constraint: SCADA integration must maintain real-time data exchange with less than 100ms latency
    and support hot-standby failover with zero data loss during primary-secondary transitions.

Constraint: Predictive maintenance models must achieve 95% recall for impending failures with
    at least 24 hours advance warning and false positive rate below 10%.

Constraint: Digital twin must maintain state synchronization with physical assets within 5 seconds
    and support what-if simulations without affecting live control systems.

Constraint: Safety instrumented systems must comply with IEC 61511 SIL 2 requirements with
    independent verification channels and fail-safe default behavior on any communication loss.

Constraint: OPC-UA communication must support Pub/Sub mode for high-frequency data and
    Client/Server mode for configuration with security profile Basic256Sha256.

Risk: SCADA communication failure blinds operators to plant status
Recovery: Activate hot-standby SCADA connection with automatic failover; switch to local
    HMI displays with last-known-good data; trigger audible alarm for operator notification

Risk: Predictive maintenance false alarm causes unnecessary production shutdown
Recovery: Require confirmation from secondary model before shutdown recommendation; provide
    confidence interval with every prediction; allow operator override with documented reasoning

Risk: Digital twin state divergence leads to incorrect simulation results
Recovery: Detect divergence through periodic checksum comparison; trigger full state
    resynchronization from physical asset; quarantine simulation results during divergence

Risk: Safety instrumented system fails to trip on dangerous condition
Recovery: Implement dual-channel safety architecture with 1-out-of-2 voting; independent
    verification via hardwired safety relay; automatic trip on communication timeout

Risk: OPC-UA server overload causes data loss during peak production periods
Recovery: Enable subscription-based data delivery to reduce polling load; apply QoS
    prioritization for safety-critical nodes; implement server-side data buffering

Risk: Cyber attack on OT network compromises industrial control systems
Recovery: Activate network segmentation and isolate affected zone; switch to manual control
    mode for critical processes; engage incident response team with forensic preservation

Layer: IndustrialIoT
    SubLayer: SCADAIntegration
    SubLayer: PredictiveMaintenance
    SubLayer: DigitalTwin
    SubLayer: SafetySystems
    SubLayer: OPCUAProtocol

Validation: SCADA data exchange latency must not exceed 100ms under normal operating conditions
Validation: Predictive maintenance predictions must include confidence score and time horizon
Validation: Digital twin state must match physical asset within 5 seconds of last sync
Validation: Safety instrumented function must trip within 500ms of dangerous condition detection
Validation: OPC-UA certificate validity must be checked before every session establishment
Validation: All control commands must pass safety interlock verification before execution
Validation: Operator actions must be logged with timestamp, identity, and rationale

# Level 2: Entities

Entity SCADAConnection
    connection_id: string
    scada_type: string
    endpoint: string
    is_primary: boolean
    is_active: boolean
    latency_ms: float
    last_data_received: datetime
    failover_pair: string

Entity EquipmentAsset
    asset_id: string
    asset_name: string
    asset_type: string
    location: string
    manufacturer: string
    install_date: datetime
    operating_hours: float
    health_score: float
    maintenance_due: datetime

Entity MaintenancePrediction
    prediction_id: string
    asset_id: string
    failure_mode: string
    estimated_failure_date: datetime
    confidence_score: float
    warning_horizon_hours: integer
    recommended_action: string
    model_version: string

Entity DigitalTwin
    twin_id: string
    asset_id: string
    state_snapshot: dict
    sync_timestamp: datetime
    divergence_score: float
    simulation_enabled: boolean
    model_fidelity: string
    last_simulation: datetime

Entity SafetyInstrumentedFunction
    function_id: string
    function_name: string
    sil_level: integer
    input_channels: list
    output_actions: list
    trip_setpoint: float
    trip_delay_ms: integer
    last_test_date: datetime
    is_active: boolean

Entity OPCUANode
    node_id: string
    browse_name: string
    data_type: string
    access_level: string
    value: any
    quality: string
    source_timestamp: datetime
    server_timestamp: datetime

# Level 3: Behaviors

Behavior ExchangeSCADAData
    Input:
        connection_id: string
        data_points: list
        direction: string
    Output:
        acknowledged_points: integer
        latency_ms: float
    Action:
        Validate SCADA connection health and latency
        Serialize data points to SCADA protocol format
        Transmit with retry logic and timeout enforcement
        Verify acknowledgment from SCADA system
        Update connection health metrics and failover readiness

Behavior PredictFailure
    Input:
        asset_id: string
        sensor_history: list
        operating_conditions: dict
    Output:
        prediction: dict
        confidence: float
        time_horizon_hours: integer
    Action:
        Extract features from sensor time series and operating conditions
        Run ensemble prediction models for each failure mode
        Aggregate predictions with weighted confidence scoring
        Generate recommended maintenance action with priority
        Validate prediction against physical constraints and plausibility

Behavior SyncDigitalTwin
    Input:
        twin_id: string
        physical_state: dict
        force_full_sync: boolean
    Output:
        sync_status: string
        divergence_score: float
    Action:
        Compare physical state with twin state snapshot
        Compute divergence score across all state dimensions
        Apply incremental update or full resynchronization
        Validate twin state consistency after update
        Enable simulation if divergence below threshold

Behavior EvaluateSafetyFunction
    Input:
        function_id: string
        input_values: dict
        override_active: boolean
    Output:
        trip_required: boolean
        trip_reason: string
        confidence: float
    Action:
        Read input channel values with dual-channel verification
        Apply safety logic with configured trip setpoint and delay
        Check for override conditions with authorization verification
        Execute trip action through independent output channels
        Log safety function evaluation with full input/output trace

Behavior BrowseOPCUANode
    Input:
        server_endpoint: string
        node_id: string
        max_depth: integer
    Output:
        node_tree: dict
        subscription_status: string
    Action:
        Establish secure OPC-UA session with certificate validation
        Browse node hierarchy up to specified depth
        Create monitored items for high-frequency data nodes
        Apply Pub/Sub configuration for bulk data delivery
        Maintain session with keepalive and automatic reconnection

# Level 4: Conditions

Condition: SCADAFailoverRequired
    When primary SCADA connection latency exceeds 500ms or connection drops
    Then initiate hot-standby failover within 2 seconds, verify data continuity,
        and alert operators with audible and visual notification

Condition: ImminentFailurePredicted
    When maintenance prediction confidence exceeds 80% and time horizon is less than 48 hours
    Then generate urgent maintenance work order, schedule production adjustment,
        and notify maintenance team with detailed failure mode analysis

Condition: DigitalTwinDivergence
    When twin divergence score exceeds 10% of state dimensions
    Then trigger full state resynchronization, disable simulation mode,
        and log divergence details for model accuracy investigation

Condition: SafetyTripActivated
    When safety instrumented function detects dangerous condition
    Then execute trip action within 500ms, activate emergency shutdown
        sequence, and notify control room with trip cause and recommended response

Condition: OPCUASecurityViolation
    When OPC-UA session certificate validation fails or unauthorized access attempted
    Then immediately terminate the session, block the client endpoint, log security
        event with full details, and alert cybersecurity operations center

# Level 5: Events

Event: SCADAFailoverCompleted
    On standby_scada_connection_activated
    Action: Verify data continuity with last-known-good comparison, update operator
        displays, and initiate primary connection recovery procedure

Event: MaintenanceAlertIssued
    On predictive_maintenance_threshold_crossed
    Action: Create maintenance work order in CMMS, schedule inspection window with
        production planning, and provide technician with diagnostic guidance

Event: TwinResyncCompleted
    On digital_twin_state_reconciled
    Action: Re-enable simulation capabilities, compute post-sync divergence score,
        and update twin fidelity metrics for model accuracy tracking

Event: SafetyTripExecuted
    On safety_instrumented_function_tripped
    Action: Log trip event with full input/output trace, trigger post-trip review
        workflow, and update safety system availability metrics

Event: OPCUAConnectionSecured
    On opcua_session_established_with_valid_certificate
    Action: Register session with monitoring, apply subscription configuration,
        and enable data flow logging for audit compliance

# Level 6: Concurrency

Parallel:
    SCADA data exchange on primary and standby connections
    Predictive maintenance model inference across all monitored assets
    Digital twin state synchronization for all active twins
    Safety instrumented function evaluation on dedicated safety controllers
    OPC-UA session management and data subscription processing
    Equipment health monitoring and alerting

# Level 7: Optimization

Optimize: Production uptime while maintaining safety compliance
    Priority: Safety instrumented function evaluation has absolute highest priority
    Priority: SCADA data exchange prioritized for safety-critical process variables
    Priority: Predictive maintenance scheduled during planned maintenance windows
    Priority: Digital twin simulation uses separate compute resources from control plane
    Priority: OPC-UA QoS configured with safety nodes at highest priority level

# Level 8: Learning

Learn: Equipment failure mode patterns from operational data
    Goal: Extend prediction horizon to 72 hours while maintaining 95% recall
    Adapt: Feature engineering and model ensemble weights per asset type
        Based: Historical failure records, sensor degradation patterns, and maintenance outcomes

Learn: Optimal maintenance scheduling around production demands
    Goal: Minimize production impact while preventing critical equipment failures
    Adapt: Maintenance window recommendations and inspection priorities
        Based: Production schedule, equipment criticality, and failure probability time series

Learn: Digital twin model fidelity improvements
    Goal: Reduce twin divergence below 2% across all state dimensions
    Adapt: Twin model parameters and synchronization frequency
        Based: Divergence measurement frequency, simulation accuracy feedback, and sensor quality

# Level 9: Security

Security:
    Encrypt: All OPC-UA communication using Basic256Sha256 security profile
    Encrypt: SCADA data channels using site-to-site VPN with AES-256
    Protect: Safety system configuration with hardware key interlock and dual authorization
    Protect: Digital twin models with access control and simulation audit logging
    Protect: Maintenance predictions with integrity verification and authorized distribution
    Encrypt: OT network traffic using MACsec at layer 2 for all industrial communications

# Level 10: Native

Native: C++
{
#include <chrono>
#include <map>
#include <vector>
#include <mutex>
#include <atomic>
#include <functional>
#include <memory>

enum class SafetyState { NORMAL, PRE_TRIP, TRIPPED, RESET_PENDING };

struct SafetyInput {
    double value;
    bool valid;
    std::chrono::system_clock::time_point timestamp;
};

struct SafetyOutput {
    bool trip_active;
    std::string trip_reason;
    std::chrono::system_clock::time_point trip_timestamp;
};

class SafetyInstrumentedFunction {
private:
    std::string function_id_;
    int sil_level_;
    double trip_setpoint_;
    int trip_delay_ms_;
    std::atomic<SafetyState> state_{SafetyState::NORMAL};
    std::map<std::string, SafetyInput> inputs_;
    std::vector<std::function<void(const SafetyOutput&)>> trip_callbacks_;
    std::mutex inputs_mutex_;
    std::chrono::system_clock::time_point pre_trip_start_;
    bool dual_channel_verified_;

public:
    SafetyInstrumentedFunction(const std::string& id, int sil,
                                double setpoint, int delay_ms)
        : function_id_(id), sil_level_(sil),
          trip_setpoint_(setpoint), trip_delay_ms_(delay_ms),
          dual_channel_verified_(false) {}

    void update_input(const std::string& channel, const SafetyInput& input) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(inputs_mutex_);
        inputs_[channel] = input;
    }

    SafetyOutput evaluate() {
        SafetyOutput output{false, "", {}};

        bool any_channel_tripped = false;
        std::string trip_channel;

        {
            std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(inputs_mutex_);
            for (const auto& [channel, input] : inputs_) {
                if (input.valid && input.value > trip_setpoint_) {
                    any_channel_tripped = true;
                    trip_channel = channel;
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        SafetyState current = state_.load();

        switch (current) {
            case SafetyState::NORMAL:
                if (any_channel_tripped) {
                    pre_trip_start_ = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
                    state_.store(SafetyState::PRE_TRIP);
                }
                break;

            case SafetyState::PRE_TRIP:
                if (!any_channel_tripped) {
                    state_.store(SafetyState::NORMAL);
                } else {
                    auto elapsed = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(
                        std::chrono::system_clock::now() - pre_trip_start_).count();
                    if (elapsed >= trip_delay_ms_) {
                        output.trip_active = true;
                        output.trip_reason = "Setpoint exceeded: " + trip_channel;
                        output.trip_timestamp = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
                        state_.store(SafetyState::TRIPPED);
                        for (const auto& cb : trip_callbacks_) {
                            cb(output);
                        }
                    }
                }
                break;

            case SafetyState::TRIPPED:
                output.trip_active = true;
                output.trip_reason = "Active trip";
                break;

            case SafetyState::RESET_PENDING:
                if (!any_channel_tripped) {
                    state_.store(SafetyState::NORMAL);
                }
                break;
        }
        return output;
    }

    void register_trip_callback(std::function<void(const SafetyOutput&)> cb) {
        trip_callbacks_.push_back(std::move(cb));
    }

    void request_reset() {
        SafetyState expected = SafetyState::TRIPPED;
        state_.compare_exchange_strong(expected, SafetyState::RESET_PENDING);
    }
};
}
